{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And his hand was holding.</b> From beforehand, while he was still in the womb, and likewise it is written: 'in the belly, עקב his brother.' The expression עקב: he explains that in the womb Jacob grasped Esau by his heel in order to hold him back so that he would not emerge first, for he was from the first drop, as Rabbi Yosi said to that matron. Therefore the birthright belonged to him, and this matter impelled him to acquire it." "<b>Sixty years old.</b> Rashi explained: he did not wish to take a shifchah. Not an actual maidservant, but an actual wife of the Canaanites — for among the Canaanites, males are called עבדים and females are called שפחות."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:55.187685825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}